
/*
QUERY NAME: Prezi and Canva External Links in Blackboard Courses

PURPOSE:
Identifies Prezi and Canva URLs referenced within Blackboard
Learn course content.

The query searches course item descriptions and STAGE JSON
data for Prezi and Canva links, identifies the course and
content item associated with each URL, and retrieves
instructor usernames.

It also counts distinct external URLs per course and
indicates whether a course contains multiple unique links.

DATA SOURCES:

1. CDM_LMS.COURSE (c)
   Contains Blackboard course information, including
   course numbers, course names, and internal identifiers.

2. CDM_LMS.COURSE_ITEM (ci)
   Contains course content items, descriptions, STAGE data,
   item types, and parent content item relationships.

3. CDM_LMS.PERSON_COURSE (pc)
   Associates users with courses and identifies
   their assigned course roles.

4. CDM_LMS.PERSON (p)
   Contains user information, including Blackboard
   usernames stored in the STAGE JSON field.

TABLE RELATIONSHIPS:

1. PERSON_COURSE.PERSON_ID = PERSON.ID
   Connects course enrollments to user records.

2. COURSE_ITEM.COURSE_ID = COURSE.ID
   Connects content items to their courses.

3. COURSE_ITEM.PARENT_COURSE_ITEM_ID = COURSE_ITEM.ID
   Connects a content item to its immediate parent item.

4. PERSON_COURSE.COURSE_ID = COURSE.ID
   Connects aggregated instructor information to courses.

COMMON TABLE EXPRESSIONS (CTEs):

The query uses three CTEs:

1. instructors
2. external_links
3. course_counts

------------------------------------------------------------
CTE 1: instructors
------------------------------------------------------------

PURPOSE:
Identifies Blackboard users assigned the Instructor role
and combines their usernames into one field per course.

INSTRUCTOR IDENTIFICATION:

pc.COURSE_ROLE = 'I'

Includes course enrollment records assigned the
Instructor role.

USERNAME EXTRACTION:

p.STAGE:user_id::string

Retrieves the Blackboard username from the PERSON.STAGE
JSON field and converts the value into a string.

LISTAGG FUNCTION:

LISTAGG(
    DISTINCT p.STAGE:user_id::string,
    ', '
)

Combines distinct instructor usernames into one
comma-separated field.

Example:
jsmith, mjones, rwilliams

DISTINCT:
Prevents repeated identical usernames from appearing
multiple times within the same course's aggregated list.

WITHIN GROUP:
Sorts usernames alphabetically within the combined field.

GROUP BY:
Produces one aggregated instructor record per COURSE_ID.

IMPORTANT:
- Multiple instructors are combined into one field.
- Instructors without a user_id in STAGE contribute
  no username to the LISTAGG result.
- The query does not filter deleted, unavailable,
  or disabled instructor enrollment records.
- The query does not filter deleted, unavailable,
  or disabled person records.
- Instructor identification is based on COURSE_ROLE = 'I',
  not PRIMARY_INSTRUCTOR_IND.

------------------------------------------------------------
CTE 2: external_links
------------------------------------------------------------

PURPOSE:
Searches course content for Prezi and Canva URLs and
extracts each matching link into a separate record.

COURSE INFORMATION:

- COURSE_KEY:
  Internal unique identifier from COURSE.ID.

- COURSE_NUMBER:
  Blackboard course number.

- COURSE_NAME:
  Name of the Blackboard course.

CONTENT ITEM INFORMATION:

- COURSE_ITEM_ID:
  Unique internal content item identifier.

- ITEM_NAME:
  Name of the Blackboard content item containing
  the external URL.

PARENT CONTENT ITEM INFORMATION:

The query uses a LEFT JOIN to connect each course
item to its immediate parent content item.

parent_ci.ID = ci.PARENT_COURSE_ITEM_ID

The following parent information is returned:

1. LEARNING_MODULE
   Name of the immediate parent content item.

2. PARENT_ITEM_TYPE
   Type of the parent content item.

3. PARENT_ITEM_TYPE_SOURCE_CODE
   Original LMS item type code for the parent.

IMPORTANT:
The LEARNING_MODULE field is an alias for the
immediate parent item's name.

The query does not verify that the parent is actually
a Blackboard Learning Module.

A parent could also be a folder or another type
of container.

Items without a matching parent will have NULL
values for the parent information.

------------------------------------------------------------
EXTERNAL URL EXTRACTION
------------------------------------------------------------

The query searches two sources within each content item:

1. COURSE_ITEM.DESCRIPTION
2. COURSE_ITEM.STAGE

SEARCH TEXT CONSTRUCTION:

COALESCE(ci.DESCRIPTION, '') || ' ' ||
COALESCE(TO_VARCHAR(ci.STAGE), '')

COALESCE:
Replaces NULL values with empty strings.

TO_VARCHAR:
Converts the STAGE JSON data into text so it can
be searched for URLs.

The two text values are combined into one string.

REGULAR EXPRESSION:

REGEXP_SUBSTR_ALL()

Searches the combined text and returns an array
containing all matching Prezi and Canva URLs.

SUPPORTED WEBSITES:

- prezi.com
- www.prezi.com
- canva.com
- www.canva.com

The expression also supports subdomains, such as:

- view.genially.prezi.com
- design.canva.com

The URL must begin with http:// or https://.

The expression requires a slash after the domain.

IMPORTANT:
- The expression searches for URL patterns.
- It does not validate whether the links work.
- It does not verify whether content is publicly
  accessible or requires authentication.
- Protocol-relative URLs beginning with //
  are not matched by this expression.
- Bare domain names without http:// or https://
  are not matched.
- URLs without a slash after the domain are not matched.

LATERAL FLATTEN:

Converts the array of extracted URLs into
individual result rows.

Examples:

- One content item with one matching URL
  produces one extracted row.

- One content item with three matching URLs
  produces three extracted rows.

- A content item with no matching URL
  produces no extracted rows.

DISTINCT:

SELECT DISTINCT removes duplicate rows where
all selected field values are identical.

IMPORTANT:
The same URL can still appear multiple times
if it belongs to different content items.

COURSE FILTER:

--WHERE c.COURSE_NUMBER ILIKE '%2026_FA'

This condition is currently commented out.

Therefore, the query searches all courses
rather than only Fall 2026 courses.

Removing the comment marker would activate
the Fall 2026 course-number filter.

NOTE:
The underscore (_) in the ILIKE pattern is a
single-character wildcard rather than a literal
underscore.

DELETION AND AVAILABILITY FILTERS:

The external_links CTE does not filter:
- Deleted courses.
- Deleted content items.
- Unavailable courses.
- Disabled courses.
- Unavailable content items.

Therefore, matching links may be returned from
records that are no longer active or available.

------------------------------------------------------------
CTE 3: course_counts
------------------------------------------------------------

PURPOSE:
Counts the number of distinct extracted Prezi and
Canva URLs associated with each course.

COUNT(DISTINCT URL):

Calculates the number of unique URL strings
identified within each course.

GROUP BY COURSE_KEY:
Produces one link count per internal course identifier.

EXAMPLE:

Course A:
- Prezi URL 1
- Prezi URL 2
- Canva URL 1

LINK_COUNT = 3

If the same Prezi URL appears in five content items,
it contributes only one unique URL to LINK_COUNT.

IMPORTANT:
LINK_COUNT measures distinct URL strings, not:
- Number of content items.
- Number of embedded presentations.
- Number of student accesses.
- Number of video or presentation views.
- Number of unique Prezi or Canva projects.

Different URL variations pointing to the same
resource may be counted separately.

------------------------------------------------------------
FINAL SELECT
------------------------------------------------------------

The final query combines:

1. External URLs and content information.
2. Aggregated instructor usernames.
3. Distinct URL counts per course.

Both supporting CTEs use LEFT JOIN.

This preserves matching external link records
even when instructor information is unavailable.

FIELDS RETURNED:

1. COURSE_ID
   Blackboard course number.

2. COURSE_NAME
   Blackboard course name.

3. INSTRUCTOR_USERNAME
   Comma-separated list of instructor usernames.

4. LINK_COUNT
   Total distinct extracted Prezi and Canva URL
   strings associated with the course.

5. MULTIPLE_LINKS
   Indicates whether the course has more than
   one distinct extracted URL.

   - YES: LINK_COUNT > 1
   - NO : LINK_COUNT <= 1

6. WEBSITE
   Identifies the website associated with the URL.

7. LEARNING_MODULE
   Name of the immediate parent content item.

8. PARENT_ITEM_TYPE
   Blackboard item type of the parent.

9. PARENT_ITEM_TYPE_SOURCE_CODE
   Original LMS item type code for the parent.

10. ITEM_NAME
    Name of the content item containing the URL.

11. URL
    Extracted Prezi or Canva URL.

------------------------------------------------------------
WEBSITE CLASSIFICATION
------------------------------------------------------------

The CASE statement classifies URLs based on domain text.

WHEN el.URL ILIKE '%prezi.com%'
    THEN 'PREZI'

WHEN el.URL ILIKE '%canva.com%'
    THEN 'CANVA'

ELSE 'OTHER'

ILIKE performs case-insensitive matching.

IMPORTANT:
The regular expression already limits extracted
URLs to Prezi and Canva domain patterns.

Therefore, the OTHER category is not expected
under normal matching conditions.

The classification is based on matching text
within the URL rather than accessing the website.

------------------------------------------------------------
MULTIPLE LINKS INDICATOR
------------------------------------------------------------

CASE
    WHEN cc.LINK_COUNT > 1 THEN 'YES'
    ELSE 'NO'
END AS MULTIPLE_LINKS

Identifies whether a course contains more than
one distinct extracted URL.

Examples:

LINK_COUNT = 1  -> NO
LINK_COUNT = 2  -> YES
LINK_COUNT = 10 -> YES

IMPORTANT:
This indicator applies to the entire course,
not the individual content item.

A course with two unique links will display
YES on every returned link record for that course.

------------------------------------------------------------
SORTING
------------------------------------------------------------

Results are ordered by:

1. COURSE_NUMBER
   Groups results by Blackboard course number.

2. WEBSITE
   Groups results by PREZI or CANVA classification.

3. LEARNING_MODULE
   Sorts by immediate parent item name.

4. ITEM_NAME
   Sorts by the content item name.

5. URL
   Sorts extracted URLs alphabetically.

------------------------------------------------------------
IMPORTANT NOTES
------------------------------------------------------------

- The query searches Prezi and Canva URLs within
  course item descriptions and STAGE data.

- The query does not search attached file contents
  or other course item fields.

- All courses are searched because the Fall 2026
  filter is currently commented out.

- Multiple instructor usernames are combined into
  one comma-separated field.

- The LEARNING_MODULE column identifies the immediate
  parent item and does not guarantee the parent is
  a Blackboard Learning Module.

- Duplicate extracted rows are removed within
  the external_links CTE using DISTINCT.

- LINK_COUNT counts unique URL strings per course.

- MULTIPLE_LINKS identifies courses containing
  more than one unique extracted URL.

- No course, enrollment, person, or content item
  deletion/availability filtering is applied.

- The query does not measure whether students
  have accessed or interacted with the links.

- The query does not confirm whether the external
  websites or presentations remain accessible.

- Results reflect external URLs stored in
  Blackboard Data - Illuminate at query time.

*/

WITH instructors AS (
    SELECT
        pc.COURSE_ID,
        LISTAGG(
            DISTINCT p.STAGE:user_id::string,
            ', '
        ) WITHIN GROUP (
            ORDER BY p.STAGE:user_id::string
        ) AS INSTRUCTOR_USERNAME
    FROM CDM_LMS.PERSON_COURSE pc
    INNER JOIN CDM_LMS.PERSON p
        ON p.ID = pc.PERSON_ID
    WHERE pc.COURSE_ROLE = 'I'
    GROUP BY pc.COURSE_ID
),

external_links AS (
    SELECT DISTINCT
        c.ID AS COURSE_KEY,
        c.COURSE_NUMBER,
        c.NAME AS COURSE_NAME,

        ci.ID AS COURSE_ITEM_ID,
        ci.NAME AS ITEM_NAME,

        parent_ci.NAME AS LEARNING_MODULE,
        parent_ci.ITEM_TYPE AS PARENT_ITEM_TYPE,
        parent_ci.ITEM_TYPE_SOURCE_CODE AS PARENT_ITEM_TYPE_SOURCE_CODE,

        f.VALUE::string AS URL

    FROM CDM_LMS.COURSE c

    INNER JOIN CDM_LMS.COURSE_ITEM ci
        ON ci.COURSE_ID = c.ID

    LEFT JOIN CDM_LMS.COURSE_ITEM parent_ci
        ON parent_ci.ID = ci.PARENT_COURSE_ITEM_ID

    , LATERAL FLATTEN(
        INPUT => REGEXP_SUBSTR_ALL(
            COALESCE(ci.DESCRIPTION, '') || ' ' ||
            COALESCE(TO_VARCHAR(ci.STAGE), ''),
            'https?://([^[:space:]\"''<>]*\\.)?(prezi\\.com|canva\\.com)/[^[:space:]\"''<>]*'
        )
    ) f

    --WHERE c.COURSE_NUMBER ILIKE '%2026_FA'
),

course_counts AS (
    SELECT
        COURSE_KEY,
        COUNT(DISTINCT URL) AS LINK_COUNT
    FROM external_links
    GROUP BY COURSE_KEY
)

SELECT
    el.COURSE_NUMBER AS COURSE_ID,
    el.COURSE_NAME,
    i.INSTRUCTOR_USERNAME,

    cc.LINK_COUNT,

    CASE
        WHEN cc.LINK_COUNT > 1 THEN 'YES'
        ELSE 'NO'
    END AS MULTIPLE_LINKS,

    CASE
        WHEN el.URL ILIKE '%prezi.com%' THEN 'PREZI'
        WHEN el.URL ILIKE '%canva.com%' THEN 'CANVA'
        ELSE 'OTHER'
    END AS WEBSITE,

    el.LEARNING_MODULE,
    el.PARENT_ITEM_TYPE,
    el.PARENT_ITEM_TYPE_SOURCE_CODE,
    el.ITEM_NAME,
    el.URL

FROM external_links el

LEFT JOIN instructors i
    ON i.COURSE_ID = el.COURSE_KEY

LEFT JOIN course_counts cc
    ON cc.COURSE_KEY = el.COURSE_KEY

ORDER BY
    el.COURSE_NUMBER,
    WEBSITE,
    el.LEARNING_MODULE,
    el.ITEM_NAME,
    el.URL;
